The Use Case Diagram provides an overall view of the interactions between the main actors and the AR-IMMS system. It identifies the major functions provided by the system and the roles responsible for performing these functions.
The AR-IMMS system has three main actors: Administrator, Technician, and Collector. The Administrator is responsible for monitoring the infrastructure and managing alerts, incidents, and tickets. The Technician performs monitoring, reviews telemetry data, handles alerts and incidents, manages maintenance tickets, and performs maintenance activities. The Technician can also use the AR application to identify devices and visualize telemetry information.
The Collector is responsible for collecting telemetry data from infrastructure devices and sending the collected data to the AR-IMMS system for processing and monitoring.
The main use cases include Login, Monitor Infrastructure, View Telemetry, Manage Alert, Manage Incident, Manage Ticket, Perform Maintenance, Identify Device Using AR, View Telemetry Using AR, Collect Telemetry, and Send Telemetry.
